'''Enllaç''' is a city in the [[Cumará (comarca)|Cumará comarca]], [[Estret Province]], [[Balboa]]. With a population of 633,727 in 2026, it is the second-largest municipality in Cumará after [[Varakí]]. Enllaç is a dense commuter suburb bordering [[Ciutat de l'Estació]], a [[ciutat]] of [[Sant Cristòfor]], to the north. The city developed along the CristoCarril Line B commuter rail corridor, which runs north–south through the municipality with four stations, and the majority of residents commute to the warehouses, factories, and railyards of Ciutat de l'Estació for work.

The city's name means "link" or "connection" in Volisanian, reflecting its role as a transit node between Sant Cristòfor and the southern Estret corridor.

== Geography ==

[[File:Enllac apartment blocks from rail line.png|thumb|250px|Apartment blocks along the CristoCarril Line B corridor in Enllaç]]

Enllaç occupies 95.3 km² on the flat lowlands of the southern Estret corridor, south of the Sant Cristòfor metropolitan area. The municipality borders [[Ciutat de l'Estació]] to the north, [[La Cruïlla]] and [[Belljardí]] to the south, [[Pla dels Horts]] to the east, and [[Mas Vell]] to the west. The terrain is generally flat, with a slight rise toward the eastern portion of the city where light industry is concentrated.

The CristoCarril Line B commuter rail line runs roughly north–south through the municipality, following the alignment of the historic Portnou Line railroad. The city's residential development is concentrated along this corridor, with the highest-density apartment blocks clustered around the four Line B stations.

=== Climate ===

Enllaç has a {{w|tropical monsoon climate}} (Köppen ''Am''), consistent with the southern Estret lowlands. Temperatures are warm year-round, with average daily highs of 30–32 °C and lows of 22–24 °C. The wet season runs from May to November, with the heaviest rainfall from June to August.

== History ==

Enllaç originated as a small settlement along the Portnou Line, the historic railroad corridor connecting Sant Cristòfor to Portnou and the canal zone. During the [[Zong Balboa]] period, the line was primarily a freight route serving the canal, and the settlement remained small. The area's growth began in earnest after the [[Adonian Community]] mandate and the post-reunification housing boom, when workers employed in the factories and railyards of Ciutat de l'Estació — then on the southern edge of the Sant Cristòfor metropolitan area — settled in Enllaç for its rail access and inexpensive land.

The establishment of CristoCarril Line B as a formal commuter rail service, with regular stops in Enllaç, transformed the settlement into a dense commuter suburb. Apartment blocks were built along the rail corridor in the 1970s and 1980s, and the population grew rapidly. The four Line B stations became the focal points of residential development, with the highest-density housing concentrated around each station.

The eastern portion of the city developed a light industrial base in the 1980s and 1990s, taking advantage of the flat terrain and the road connection to the canal corridor. Food processing, small-scale manufacturing, and logistics operations established themselves in this area, providing some local employment alongside the commuter economy.

== Government ==

Enllaç is governed by an elected {{w|mayor}} and a municipal council. The mayor serves four-year terms and has executive authority over municipal administration, planning, and local services. The current mayor is [[Jordi Mas i Sòria]] of the [[Socialist Front of Balboa]] (FSB), elected in 2024. Mas i Sòria, a former trade union organiser from the eastern industrial district, campaigned on affordable transit fares, tenant protections, and investment in the eastern neighbourhoods. The FSB's strong base in Enllaç reflects the city's working-class commuter population and industrial workforce.

== Demographics ==

Enllaç's population of 633,727 (2026) makes it the second-largest municipality in the Cumará comarca. The population is predominantly working-class, with a large proportion of residents employed in the warehouses, factories, and railyards of neighbouring [[Ciutat de l'Estació]]. The city's ethnic composition is diverse, with a large [[Black Balboan people|Black Balboan]] majority and significant [[Mixed Balboan people|mixed]] and [[Fosian Balboan people|Fosian]] communities. The population is younger than the Estret average, and household sizes are larger, consistent with the working-class family housing stock.

== Economy ==

Enllaç's economy is based on commuting and local services. The majority of the working population commutes northward to [[Ciutat de l'Estació]] via CristoCarril Line B, where they are employed in the warehouses, factories, and rail operations that characterise that ciutat. The four Line B stations serve as the primary commuter nodes, with morning and evening peak ridership concentrated at the northern stations closest to the Sant Cristòfor border.

The eastern portion of the city contains a light industrial zone with food processing, small-scale manufacturing, and logistics operations. This area provides some local employment, though the majority of Enllaç residents work outside the municipality. The residential corridors along the rail line support a retail and service economy of small shops, restaurants, and local businesses clustered around the station areas.

== Transport ==

=== Commuter rail ===

{{main|CristoCarril}}

CristoCarril Line B, operated by [[Intercon]], is the primary transport service in Enllaç. The line runs north–south through the municipality, connecting Enllaç to [[Ciutat de l'Estació]] and the Sant Cristòfor rail network to the north, and to the southern Cumará corridor toward [[Varakí]] and [[Areza]] to the south. Line B has four stations within Enllaç, each serving as a focal point for residential development:

