=== Bus ===

The city bus network provides feeder connections to the four Line B stations and serves the eastern industrial zone and the lower-density residential areas between the rail corridors. Bus routes also connect Enllaç to the surrounding municipalities in the Cumará comarca, including [[Mas Vell]], [[Pla dels Horts]], and [[Belljardí]].

=== Roads ===

Enllaç is connected to the Sant Cristòfor metropolitan road network via the northern border with Ciutat de l'Estació. The canal corridor road runs through the eastern portion of the city, providing access to the industrial zone and connecting to the broader Estret Province road network. Local roads link the residential corridors along the rail line to the eastern industrial area and the neighbouring municipalities.

== Neighbourhoods ==

Enllaç is broadly divided into two zones:

=== Rail Corridor ===

The rail corridor is the residential heart of Enllaç, running north–south along the CristoCarril Line B alignment. The highest-density apartment blocks are clustered around the four Line B stations, with density decreasing with distance from the tracks. The housing stock consists predominantly of mid-rise apartment blocks built in the 1970s and 1980s, with some newer infill development. The rail corridor is the most ethnically diverse part of the city and the focus of its commercial and social life, with small shops, restaurants, and services concentrated around the station areas.

=== Eastern Industrial Zone ===

The eastern portion of Enllaç contains the city's light industrial base, with food processing facilities, small-scale manufacturing, and logistics operations. The area is separated from the residential corridors by a buffer of lower-density housing and green space. Workers' housing is interspersed with the industrial plots, particularly along the road connections to the canal corridor. The industrial zone is the primary source of local employment within Enllaç, though it employs only a fraction of the city's working population.

== Notable places ==

* '''Enllaç Nord station''' — the busiest CristoCarril Line B station in Enllaç, serving commuters to Ciutat de l'Estació
* '''Enllaç Centre station''' — the civic and commercial hub of the city
* '''Eastern Industrial Zone''' — light manufacturing and food processing district

